.el .ds Aq '
.TH mdmc-decompile 1  "decompile " 
.SH NAME
mdmc\-decompile \- Decompile a message to a markdown snapshot note
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmdmc decompile\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-stdout\fR] [\fB\-\-link\-attachments\fR] [\fB\-\-link\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decompile a message to a markdown snapshot note
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config.toml (default ~/.config/mdmc/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-stdout\fR
Print the note to stdout instead of writing to [paths] snapshots
.TP
\fB\-\-link\-attachments\fR
Append an `## Attachments` section listing extracted files
.TP
\fB\-\-link\-format\fR \fI<LINK_FORMAT>\fR
Emit inline images as wikilinks (![[...]]) or markdown (![](...))
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
wikilink
.IP \(bu 2
markdown
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Message\-ID, a raw message file path, or `\-` for stdin
